cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AuditPledge, please cite it as below."
title: "AuditPledge: Provenance and Priced Risk for the MCP Tools a Compound Agent Calls"
authors:
  - family-names: Sarkar
    given-names: Dipankar
year: 2026
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/doom2quake/auditpledge"
repository-code: "https://github.com/doom2quake/auditpledge"
abstract: >-
  AuditPledge audits the Model Context Protocol tool supply chain of a
  Compound-facing AI agent. It opens a real MCP session, verifies Ed25519
  provenance for every tool against a committed public keyring, scores the
  supply-chain risk weighted for what a Compound position exposes (state reads,
  transaction building, collateral movement), and prices the residual risk into an
  expected loss and a suggested premium so a risk owner can act on a dollar figure.
  A counterfactual pass reruns the identical scorer over a mutated manifest so the
  saving from a fix is measured, not asserted. Everything ambiguous fails closed.
  A candidate entry to the Compound Grants Program, Security Tooling domain.
  Testnet and seeded only.
